%I A402502 #15 Nov 22 2026 12:33:10
%S A402502 7,7,31,631,2311,30031,510511,29099071,223092871,6469693231,
%T A402502 601681470391,22262214404431,912750790581631,13082761331670031,
%U A402502 1844669347765474231,97767475431570134191,1922760350154212639071,117288381359406970983271,23574964653240801167637271,557940830126698960967415391
%N A402502 a(n) is the number equal to either prime(n)# + 1 (A006862) or 3*prime(n)# + 1 (A402501) that is congruent to 7 modulo 8, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402502 For n >= 1, a(n) == 7 (mod 8) is a quadratic residue modulo every prime 3 <= p <= prime(n).
%C A402502 By requiring a(n) == 7 (mod 8), sequence forms a compatible system modulo {A102476(n+1)=4*prime(n)#}: a(n) mod 4*prime(m)# = a(m) for n >= m >= 1.
%C A402502 Let N = A102476(n+1) be the least modulus with 2^(n+1) square roots of 1. The minimal element of the coset of (Z/NZ)*^2 in (Z/NZ)* containing a(n), or the least m coprime to N such that a(n)/m is a square modulo N, is m = A402507(n-1). Here (Z/NZ)* is the multiplicative group of integers modulo N and (Z/NZ)*^2 is the subgroup of squares.
%C A402502 For any fundamental discriminant D of a quadratic field dividing N, kronecker(D,a(n)) = -1 if and only if D == 4 (mod 8) or D == 24 (mod 32).
%H A402502 Jianing Song, <a href="/A402502/b402502.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..350</a>
%F A402502 Let b(n) = A267098(n) = A066490(prime(n)) be the number of primes p <= prime(n) that are congruent to 3 modulo 4. Then a(n) = prime(n)# + 1 if b(n) is odd and 3*prime(n)# + 1 if b(n) is even.
%o A402502 (PARI) my(P=1, pi43=0); forprime(p=2, 100, P*=p; if(p%4==3, pi43=1-pi43); print1(if(pi43==1, P+1, 3*P+1), ", "); )
%Y A402502 Cf. A002110, A102476, A006862, A402501, A066490, A267098, A402507.
%Y A402502 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402502 nonn,easy,new
%O A402502 1,1
